::PC_U04_L02_Q_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U04_L02_Q_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.2
Question:
Which statement describes the circle (x-1)² + (y--1)² = 9
{
=A. Center (1,-1) and radius 3#Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
~B. Center (-1,--1) and radius 9#This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
~C. Center (3,3) and radius 1#This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~D. Center (1,-1) and diameter 3#This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
}

